# Complete read/add flow for VS Code REST Client.
# Start the backend: cd D:\bookmg-workspace\bookmg-repo-be ; npm.cmd run dev
# Run requests from top to bottom using "Send Request" above each block.
# POST, PATCH, and DELETE requests below change your local shelf.
# All requests use our backend; the frontend never needs to call Open Library.
# Verified Open Library sample (2026-09-30):
# Work OL27482W = The Hobbit; edition OL61641547M belongs to it and has 306 pages.
# Open Library's Search year is 1937, while its Work first_publish_date is
# "January 1938". The backend detail/add responses use the Work value (1938).
# Public metadata can change; the IDs and expected values here are sample data.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:3000
@workId = OL27482W
@editionId = OL61641547M
@coverId = 14627509

### 1. Confirm the backend is running: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### 2. Search by title: 200; find OL27482W in data and note isInShelf
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/search?q=The%20Hobbit&field=title&page=1&limit=20

### 3. Read normalized details: 200; editionId OL61641547M, totalPages 306
### If the work is already in your shelf, saved edition/pages take precedence.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/{{workId}}

### 4. Fetch its cover through the backend: 200 image/jpeg
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/covers/{{coverId}}

### 5. Add it as want-to-read: first request 201; later requests 409
### This writes to MySQL.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workId": "{{workId}}",
  "editionId": "{{editionId}}"
}

### 5a. Start reading: 200; startedAt is recorded
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf/{{workId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "reading"
}

### 6. Read details again: 200; isInShelf true, saved totalPages 306
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/{{workId}}

### 7. List all shelf books, newest first: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf

### 8. Show reading books only: 200; The Hobbit should appear
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf?status=reading

### 9. Show finished books only: 200; may be empty
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf?status=finished

### 10. Count all books and statuses: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf/stats

### 11. Confirm duplicate protection: 409 BOOK_ALREADY_IN_SHELF
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workId": "{{workId}}",
  "editionId": "{{editionId}}"
}

### 12. Record progress, rating, and notes: 200; currentPage 75
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf/{{workId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPage": 75,
  "rating": 5,
  "notes": "A good read"
}

### 13. Reach the known page count: 200; status becomes finished
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf/{{workId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPage": 306
}

### 14. Counts now include one more finished book
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf/stats

### 15. Resume reading: 200; clears finishedAt and keeps startedAt
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf/{{workId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPage": 120
}

### 16. Invalid progress: 400 VALIDATION_ERROR; stored page remains 120
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf/{{workId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPage": 307
}

### 17. Optional: remove from shelf after confirming in the UI
### This deletes both the shelf entry and book metadata in one transaction.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf/{{workId}}

### 18. Confirm it is gone from the shelf
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf?status=reading

### 19. Repeating the delete returns 404 SHELF_ENTRY_NOT_FOUND
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/shelf/{{workId}}

### Optional: compare your existing Harry Potter entry; saved page count may be null
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/books/OL82563W
